  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Acts",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 26,
    "summary": "Paul recounts his former persecution of the Saints as a Pharisee—He testifies of the appearance of Jesus on the Damascus road—Paul bears his testimony to King Agrippa.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then Agrippa said unto Paul, Thou art permitted to speak for thyself. Then Paul stretched forth the hand, and answered for himself:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:1",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "I think myself happy, king Agrippa, because I shall answer for myself this day before thee touching all the things whereof I am accused of the Jews:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:2",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Especially because I know thee to be expert in all customs and questions which are among the Jews: wherefore I beseech thee to hear me patiently.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:3",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "My manner of life from my youth, which was at the first among mine own nation at Jerusalem, know all the Jews;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:4",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Which knew me from the beginning, if they would testify, that after the most straitest sect of our religion I lived a Pharisee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 126,
            "text": "Acts 22:3; 23:6 (6–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:5",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And now I stand and am judged for the hope of the promise made of God unto our fathers:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:6",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto which promise our twelve tribes, instantly serving God day and night, hope to come. For which hope’s sake, king Agrippa, I am accused of the Jews.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Israel, Twelve Tribes of."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "GR earnestly, intently."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Israel, Twelve Tribes of.",
            "prettyString": "TG Israel, Twelve Tribes of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Israel, Twelve Tribes of",
                "entryId": "tg-israel-twelve-tribes-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:7",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Why should it be thought a thing incredible with you, that God should raise the dead?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Resurrection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Resurrection.",
            "prettyString": "TG Resurrection",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Resurrection",
                "entryId": "tg-resurrection",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:8",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "I verily thought with myself, that I ought to do many things contrary to the name of Jesus of Nazareth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "1 Tim. 1:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Name."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Tim. 1:13.",
            "prettyString": "1 Timothy 1:13",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1timothy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
