        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:10",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And I punished them oft in every synagogue, and compelled them to blaspheme; and being exceedingly mad against them, I persecuted them even unto strange cities.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 152,
            "text": "GR foreign."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62
          },
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 134
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:11",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Whereupon as I went to Damascus with authority and commission from the chief priests,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:12",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "At midday, O king, I saw in the way a light from heaven, above the brightness of the sun, shining round about me and them which journeyed with me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "JS—H 1:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "JS—H 1:16.",
            "prettyString": "JS—H 1:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "josephsmithhistory",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:13",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And when we were all fallen to the earth, I heard a voice speaking unto me, and saying in the Hebrew tongue, Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me? it is hard for thee to kick against the pricks.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 113,
            "text": "Acts 9:4 (1–9); 22:7 (6–16)."
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 181,
            "text": "TG Opposition."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 146,
            "end": 151
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Opposition.",
            "prettyString": "TG Opposition",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Opposition",
                "entryId": "tg-opposition",
                "book": "",
