        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:20",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "For these causes the Jews caught me in the temple, and went about to kill me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Acts 21:31 (30–31)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 26:21",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Having therefore obtained help of God, I continue unto this day, witnessing both to small and great, saying none other things than those which the prophets and Moses did say should come:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 155,
            "text": "Acts 28:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Acts 28:23.",
            "prettyString": "Acts 28:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
